   299	`sigma` to the normalization (`l` is smooth, being a component of a tree of
   300	rational curves, so the lift exists).  Define
   301	
   302	```text
   303	mu_l := mult_l ( Phi^* Gamma ),                                    (4.0)
   304	```
   305	
   306	the coefficient of `l` in the pullback of the divisor `Gamma`.  It is a
   307	positive integer because `l subset Phi^{-1}(Gamma)`.
   308	
   309	**Proposition 4.1 (local degree along `l`).**
   310	(a) For every `p in l` outside a finite set, `mult_p(Phi) = mu_l`.  Hence
   311	`mu_l` *is* the generic local degree, i.e. the Orevkov base multiplicity
